Project 1: AI Config Builder for Microservices
Overview
The AI Config Builder for Microservices is an automated two-stage AI pipeline designed to assist DevOps and SRE teams in generating and validating Kubernetes infrastructure configuration files from natural-language prompts. Built using Python, OpenAI API (gpt-5.6-luna), and PyYAML, this tool bridges the gap between high-level architectural descriptions and syntactically sound cluster manifests.

Features
Natural-Language-to-IaC Translation: Automatically transforms conversational prompt specifications into valid Kubernetes Deployment YAML.

Automated Syntax Validation: Leverages Python's yaml module to perform robust pre-deployment schema and syntax checks.

Deterministic Code Generation: Configured with strict generation parameters (temperature=0.2) to maintain structured, predictable output.

